WEBVTT

00:37.552 --> 00:40.720
- Hey, how'd you sleep, Peter?
- Brian, last night I had this crazy dream.

00:40.804 --> 00:43.057
I was eating a sheep
and now my pillow's gone.

00:43.182 --> 00:45.936
Oh, wait. Here it is.
What the hell was I eating?

00:50.105 --> 00:51.732
Oh, sorry.

01:07.663 --> 01:08.706
See you, Lois.

01:08.789 --> 01:12.042
And like I tell you every day, if I come
back in the middle of the afternoon

01:12.126 --> 01:14.961
and you're having sex with somebody,
I'll kill you both.

01:15.547 --> 01:19.591
"Thanks to effective treatments,
Magic Johnson down to one AID."

01:20.842 --> 01:24.554
Oh, God, did I hit that deaf kid again?
They ought to put a bell on that guy.

01:27.266 --> 01:30.602
The nurse says Brian won't be out
of surgery for another three hours.

01:30.685 --> 01:33.230
- Oh, I hope he's gonna be okay.
- Me, too.

01:33.313 --> 01:36.191
I know we're not here to place blame
or beat ourselves up, but,

01:36.316 --> 01:39.361
I can't help feeling like
this is somehow Meg's fault.

01:39.486 --> 01:42.113
Oh, I just can't stand the thought
of losing Brian.

01:42.196 --> 01:45.533
If he dies, I'm gonna have
to start hanging out with The Rock again.

01:45.658 --> 01:50.495
<i>One's a baby,
and the other's black, I think.</i>

01:50.831 --> 01:54.166
<i>At least part black. Or Hispanic.</i>

01:54.833 --> 01:57.503
<i>I think, you know, possibly,
there's some Filipino in there.</i>

01:57.628 --> 01:59.548
<i>Yeah, possibly some Filipino.</i>

01:59.963 --> 02:03.342
<i>I mean, if he, if he's black,
it's definitely diluted.</i>

02:04.050 --> 02:06.511
<i>I mean, one of his parents must be white.</i>

02:06.887 --> 02:10.098
<i>What the hell is Jessica Alba,
for that matter?</i>

02:10.848 --> 02:14.477
<i>If I were 40 years younger,
I would plow that till next July.</i>

02:17.064 --> 02:20.025
All right, class, today as a special treat,
I'm going to show you this

02:20.108 --> 02:22.861
<i>fascinating episode of NOVA
that I taped at home for you.</i>

02:24.904 --> 02:26.447
You coming back to bed, Rob?

02:26.530 --> 02:28.949
Hang on, honey. Hang on.
My jaw keeps locking up.

02:29.033 --> 02:31.160
<i>Well, that's not NOVA at all, is it?</i>

02:32.203 --> 02:34.496
That's a sex tape I made with my wife.

02:34.580 --> 02:37.498
Of course, nobody here is interested
in seeing that sort of thing.

02:37.582 --> 02:39.334
Are they? Probably not. No.

02:39.418 --> 02:42.171
Okay. You kind of looked like
you were nodding? Nope?

02:42.296 --> 02:43.838
Okay. Okay, we should get back to work.

02:43.963 --> 02:46.508
All right, next up,
does everyone have a lab partner?

02:46.592 --> 02:47.884
- I don't.
- Me, neither.

02:48.009 --> 02:48.967
She can be my partner.

02:49.051 --> 02:52.096
Sarah, that's very irresponsible.
Meg is awful.

02:52.514 --> 02:54.265
- You want to be my lab partner?
- Really?

02:54.391 --> 02:55.517
Sure, you seem nice.

02:55.600 --> 02:57.559
Hey, do you want
to join my after-school club?

02:57.684 --> 02:58.644
Sure.

02:58.770 --> 03:01.020
Now, open your books to page...
You know what? Look, I'm sorry.

03:01.103 --> 03:03.231
Can I just go ahead and show this video
of me doing my wife?

03:05.567 --> 03:07.737
Here we are, Brian, safe and sound.

03:07.861 --> 03:11.157
- Peter, I don't need to be in a wheelchair.
- Now, now, no arguments, Brian.

03:11.239 --> 03:14.033
I already went through the trouble
of borrowing this ramp from Joe.

03:14.158 --> 03:16.577
I'll see you, honey. I'll be back in a...

03:16.912 --> 03:18.413
Joe, are you all right?

03:18.538 --> 03:21.540
Don't help me up.
I need to retain my independence.

03:22.583 --> 03:25.211
- You need anything from the market?
- PowerBar!

03:28.173 --> 03:29.382
What's wrong, Brian?

03:29.465 --> 03:32.926
You've just been sitting on the couch
ever since you got back from the hospital.

03:33.052 --> 03:34.719
You need to get out of the house.

03:34.845 --> 03:36.765
I don't know, Lois. I'm a little depressed.

03:36.848 --> 03:39.475
The accident got me thinking
about how uncertain life is

03:39.599 --> 03:41.392
and how suddenly it can be taken away.

03:41.476 --> 03:43.561
You're going to feel back to normal
in no time.

03:43.686 --> 03:45.939
- Here, have some food.
- I'm not hungry.

03:46.064 --> 03:47.774
Here comes the gravy.

03:51.570 --> 03:53.404
You messy beast.

03:56.573 --> 03:58.242
Well, hello there, Meg.

03:58.827 --> 04:01.079
Neil, I really can't be seen talking
to you anymore.

04:01.204 --> 04:03.831
I have friends now,
and some of them, very popular.

04:03.955 --> 04:06.710
I know. I heard Sarah is your lab partner.

04:06.792 --> 04:09.879
All those years of you rejecting me
finally made sense.

04:09.962 --> 04:11.254
What do you mean?

04:14.925 --> 04:17.177
Oh, my God!

04:23.390 --> 04:25.102
Meg! There you are.

04:25.185 --> 04:27.646
Hey, everybody,
this is our newest member, Meg.

04:27.770 --> 04:28.938
- Hi, Meg.
- What's up?

04:29.022 --> 04:31.107
Hi, you gays, guys. Girls.

04:31.816 --> 04:35.695
Look, listen, Sarah, I can't be in your club.
I'm not a lesbian.

04:35.820 --> 04:38.823
You can't be serious.
We had a whole party planned for you.

04:38.947 --> 04:41.116
Really? A party, for me?

04:41.243 --> 04:44.203
- But I guess if you're not a lesbian...
- Wait, wait.

04:44.327 --> 04:46.621
You didn't let me finish. I'm not a lesbian.

04:46.746 --> 04:49.041
I'm a super, huge mega-lesbian.

04:49.165 --> 04:51.876
Good.
You'll fit in with the other mega-lesbians.

05:07.558 --> 05:09.851
Wow! I feel so socially accepted.

05:09.977 --> 05:13.021
Hey, do you have any other friends
you want to invite to your party?

05:13.147 --> 05:16.274
No. Most of my friends are out of town.

05:16.567 --> 05:20.446
Oh, this is gonna be great!
We'll stay up late, trade stories.

05:21.362 --> 05:24.157
Let's watch the video of my ballet recital.

05:25.534 --> 05:26.825
Here it is!

05:29.746 --> 05:31.998
Sunshine Bear. Wait!

05:43.051 --> 05:45.010
- Hey, how's it going?
- Good.

05:45.134 --> 05:46.846
Those are huge.

05:46.929 --> 05:50.224
Those are huge boobs.
And you know what's nice?

05:50.349 --> 05:54.519
That you don't have that blue vein
up there that some of the bigger ones get.

05:55.730 --> 05:58.606
What? I said you don't have that.

05:58.731 --> 06:03.276
- Hey, buddy, you're not looking so good.
- Who cares how I look? Nothing matters.

06:03.402 --> 06:05.696
We could all die tomorrow,
every one of us.

06:05.821 --> 06:08.658
Well, isn't that a damn good reason
to live it up today?

06:08.741 --> 06:13.079
- Come on, it can't possibly be that simple.
- Excuse me. I got a thing to do.

06:13.747 --> 06:16.582
<i>All right, ladies and gentlemen,
we have a very special guest tonight.</i>

06:16.707 --> 06:21.128
<i>Please welcome the Member of the Board,
Frank Sinatra Jr.</i>

06:58.746 --> 07:01.749
All this singing is contagious. I'll sing, too.

07:07.547 --> 07:09.258
A little bit softer now.

07:17.639 --> 07:20.101
I'll come out when they're all gone.

07:24.563 --> 07:27.775
Wow, Brian, you actually got
to sing with Frank Sinatra Jr?

07:27.900 --> 07:28.942
Oh, it was amazing.

07:29.026 --> 07:32.655
I got to tell you, he said some things
that were exactly what I needed to hear,

07:32.779 --> 07:35.156
and I was just inspired
to get up on that stage.

07:35.282 --> 07:37.492
Got to live life for today, you know?

07:37.616 --> 07:40.828
Brian, don't you think it's a little too early
to be hitting the booze?

07:40.954 --> 07:42.079
Hey, what's the point of waiting?

07:42.163 --> 07:44.124
You got to live life while you can
and live it hard.

07:44.208 --> 07:45.792
The Chris Farley method, that's good.

07:45.875 --> 07:47.501
Frank invited me back this evening.

07:47.627 --> 07:51.005
I tell you, I feel more exhilarated than
Peter did when he swam with the bulls.

08:16.070 --> 08:18.155
Yeah, that's fair.
No, that's totally a fair score.

08:23.368 --> 08:27.665
You know, Brian, when you wear that suit,
it looks like you're taking a white poop.

08:28.625 --> 08:29.707
But it's stuck.

08:29.833 --> 08:32.837
Look, Lois asked me to baby-sit you,
so just stay here and be quiet.

08:32.920 --> 08:34.923
I'll be back after my first set.

08:37.299 --> 08:39.761
What the hell am I supposed
to do to kill time?

08:40.220 --> 08:42.011
Oh, maybe I'll play 52 Pickup.

08:43.639 --> 08:45.933
This game's better
if there's someone else here.

08:46.058 --> 08:48.935
'Cause then they can say,
"I'm not going to pick up those cards. "

08:49.060 --> 08:52.230
And then I say,
"You have to, it's 52 Pickup. "

08:52.356 --> 08:55.149
And they say,
"Well, what if I just leave them there?"

08:55.232 --> 08:58.862
And I say, " Those are my father's cards.
You can't just leave them there.

08:58.944 --> 09:00.404
"He's going to be mad. "

09:00.655 --> 09:01.655
Where am I?

09:12.749 --> 09:14.000
Get out of here.

09:25.343 --> 09:28.681
Whoa. Easy, kid. These people paid
good money to get in here.

09:28.765 --> 09:31.267
Oh, yeah? How much
are you charging them to get out?

09:50.285 --> 09:51.453
That was sensational.

09:51.578 --> 09:54.248
We're going to be the biggest thing
since Edison harnessed electricity.

09:57.124 --> 09:59.878
Look at Edison over there
with his damn electricity.

09:59.961 --> 10:02.755
Hey, Edison, how about sharing some
of those light bulbs, huh?

10:02.880 --> 10:06.799
- Hey, figure it out for yourself, man.
- We're freezing our asses off over here.

10:06.925 --> 10:08.886
Hey, man, how do you think I feel,
you know?

10:08.970 --> 10:12.223
You get to look at my great house.
I get to look at that dark thing, huh?

10:12.307 --> 10:14.725
What, what is that, a candle over there?
That's pretty sweet.

10:14.809 --> 10:17.311
Yeah, it's a candle.
We're freezing over here.

10:17.394 --> 10:20.772
No one in my family's taken a bath
in a month. We stink.

10:20.855 --> 10:22.107
It stinks over here, you jerk.

10:22.190 --> 10:23.609
I can't hear you over my central heating.

10:23.692 --> 10:26.193
- Hey, why don't you go to hell, Edison.
- Hey, bite me, man.

10:26.319 --> 10:27.569
<i>Hey, you guys seen The Office?</i>

10:27.653 --> 10:29.782
Oh, no, I guess you haven't
'cause you don't have a TV.

10:29.906 --> 10:31.825
Hey, how about I come over there
and kick your ass?

10:31.949 --> 10:33.492
Yeah, come on over.

10:43.752 --> 10:47.298
- What is this, Lois?
- It's jambalaya. It's a new recipe.

10:50.300 --> 10:53.721
Peter. Eat your food, mister.

10:54.220 --> 10:56.681
All right, if you don't want it,
put it in your napkin.

10:56.805 --> 11:00.811
Peter, put it in your napkin!
Put it in your...

11:00.936 --> 11:03.145
I'm not gonna...

11:03.521 --> 11:06.440
You know, some people would
be very happy to have this food.

11:06.523 --> 11:07.942
Like John Goodman's family.

11:09.109 --> 11:10.278
Please, Daddy.

11:10.361 --> 11:13.697
I told you, when I'm finished,
you can have what's left.

11:13.821 --> 11:17.492
There won't be any left.
There's never any left.

11:21.872 --> 11:23.456
Happy Thanksgiving.

11:27.961 --> 11:29.754
Mom, why is the cable guy here?

11:29.879 --> 11:32.923
It's me, you guys,
and I have something to tell you all.

11:33.050 --> 11:36.470
Mom. Dad. I am a lesbian.

11:37.721 --> 11:40.681
- That is awesome.
- Peter.

11:40.764 --> 11:42.851
Meg, you are not a lesbian.

11:42.934 --> 11:44.684
You know, I don't care
what you guys think.

11:44.810 --> 11:48.523
All my new lesbian friends accept me,
and that's all that matters.

11:48.606 --> 11:51.276
Meg, you're my daughter.
I would accept you if you were gay

11:51.400 --> 11:53.569
or blind or retarded, but you're not.

11:53.695 --> 11:57.739
You guys don't care about me
and my struggle! I hate you!

11:57.864 --> 12:01.743
Meg, I think you're just trying to fit in
by pretending to be something you're not.

12:01.827 --> 12:04.912
Like the time Peter pretended
to be racist to get out of jury duty.

12:08.166 --> 12:10.376
Awful lot of honkies in here.

12:48.787 --> 12:51.957
Brian, there you are.
Do you have any idea what time it is?

12:52.083 --> 12:54.209
Stewie was supposed
to be in bed two hours ago.

12:54.293 --> 12:57.587
Oh, yeah, he... He's...

12:57.712 --> 13:00.424
He was right here,
right next to me like, four hours ago.

13:00.507 --> 13:03.509
What? Brian,
you were supposed to watch him!

13:03.634 --> 13:07.431
- Oh, my little sweetie!
- Hey, Brian, remember me?

13:07.556 --> 13:09.224
I'm the guy you left standing
at the counter

13:09.308 --> 13:11.809
at McDonald's with a bag full of burgers.

13:11.892 --> 13:14.479
You know, it's funny,
I tried to walk home and...

13:14.771 --> 13:18.441
A lot of hungry deer walking around
at this hour of the night and...

13:18.524 --> 13:22.612
Oh, here's where the story gets fun.
You may have noticed I'm missing an ear.

13:22.696 --> 13:27.158
Managed to pull it out of the deer's mouth
and put it in some ice I got at a 7-Eleven.

13:27.241 --> 13:30.243
So, when you're ready to apologize,
just talk into this cup.

13:30.326 --> 13:32.246
Brian, this is inexcusable.

13:32.330 --> 13:34.122
Yeah, what if something
had happened to Stewie?

13:34.206 --> 13:36.123
My ear's in a cup,
I guess that doesn't count.

13:36.207 --> 13:39.085
Hey, I'm not the kid's baby-sitter,
all right? I have my own life to live.

13:39.169 --> 13:42.506
You know, this is all because you've been
hanging out with that Frank Sinatra Jr.

13:42.631 --> 13:46.176
I am gonna call his mother Mia Farrow
and give her a piece of my mind.

13:46.300 --> 13:48.343
And you are gonna stop singing
at that crazy club.

13:48.678 --> 13:51.474
- Operator, Mia Farrow, please.
- You stay out of my life!

13:54.183 --> 13:56.018
What the hell is happening to you?

13:56.143 --> 13:58.562
Yeah, don't worry, I don't need to go
to the hospital or anything.

13:58.687 --> 14:00.480
I'll just use this Mr. Potato Head piece.

14:04.776 --> 14:09.239
- He bit me, Lois. The bastard bit me.
- Oh, honey, I'm sure he didn't mean it.

14:09.365 --> 14:13.201
Brian's going through some heavy stuff
right now. He almost died.

14:15.621 --> 14:17.330
Listen, Peter, I...

14:17.956 --> 14:20.499
I just want to apologize.
You know what? Forget it.

14:20.625 --> 14:22.751
I don't need this.
I'm out of here.

14:23.251 --> 14:24.796
Look what you did, Peter.

14:24.878 --> 14:28.341
I can't help it. I haven't been this scared
since I was mugged by Gene Shalit.

14:28.465 --> 14:30.259
<i>Don't Panic Room.</i>

14:30.385 --> 14:33.305
I'm not going to William Hurt you.

14:33.554 --> 14:36.431
<i>I only want your Tango & Cash.</i>

14:36.808 --> 14:38.726
<i>So just Pay It Forward</i>

14:38.851 --> 14:41.936
<i>and we'll all be Happy Gilmore.</i>

14:42.270 --> 14:43.229
What?

14:47.734 --> 14:50.737
So, how's my suddenly
lesbian daughter doing?

14:50.863 --> 14:55.741
Great. We're checking out naked girls.
I am so into girls.

14:55.908 --> 14:58.411
Oh, come on, Meg,
you can stop the charade.

14:58.494 --> 15:00.955
My God, you're as transparent
as your father was

15:01.080 --> 15:03.542
when he pretended to be
a Hasidic Jew to get off work.

15:03.832 --> 15:07.879
Good morning, Hebrews and shebrews.
What a glorious Jewish day.

15:08.004 --> 15:11.049
Hey, how about all those coupons
in the Sunday paper, huh?

15:11.172 --> 15:12.716
Some good deals there.

15:12.799 --> 15:16.386
Hey, you know, I went into a store
last week and they wanted $800 for a TV,

15:16.511 --> 15:19.013
but I us'ed them down to $500.

15:20.808 --> 15:24.101
It's not a charade, Mom. I am a lesbian.

15:24.227 --> 15:25.937
What do I have to do to prove this to you?

15:26.062 --> 15:28.523
Well, maybe if I'd seen you
kiss your girlfriend.

15:28.607 --> 15:30.732
- Fine.
- What was that?

15:30.858 --> 15:32.861
What is she, your grandmother?

15:32.944 --> 15:35.239
That's no kiss. Watch this.

15:42.285 --> 15:44.413
Look, I can't tell you how to lead your life.

15:44.497 --> 15:48.333
If you don't want to face the truth,
there's nothing I can do about it.

15:49.126 --> 15:52.130
Chris, I'm all out of digital audio tape.
Oh, he's gone.

15:52.255 --> 15:54.213
Hey, can I get you guys
to sign these release forms?

15:56.966 --> 16:00.260
- Oh, where the hell is Brian?
- I don't know, but I better go find him.

16:00.386 --> 16:02.680
We can't sit here watching
infomercials all night.

16:02.805 --> 16:04.975
<i>Hello. How come I rich and you not?</i>

16:05.099 --> 16:07.268
<i>How come you not sell real estate
like I do?</i>

16:07.393 --> 16:09.228
<i>How come I sleep with your wife
while you at work</i>

16:09.312 --> 16:11.731
<i>and then I pee in your toilet
and don't flush?</i>

16:11.815 --> 16:15.109
<i>And sometimes I open the back part and
I pee in there, so that when you flush</i>

16:15.192 --> 16:17.319
<i>pee come out. You know why?
Because I'm smart.</i>

16:17.445 --> 16:19.404
<i>I'm smart, you're stupid. Call now.</i>

16:19.863 --> 16:23.617
Brian! Brian!

16:23.909 --> 16:27.580
Brian! Brian...

16:28.872 --> 16:33.000
Who am I kidding? All those buttons,
I'll look like Steve Harvey. Brian!

16:36.336 --> 16:38.839
Yeah, I'll ask the cashier
if I can put this up in the window.

16:39.131 --> 16:43.635
I definitely need a breath freshener.
But that's going to give me 11 items.

16:43.968 --> 16:45.930
- That's fine.
- No, no, no.

16:46.013 --> 16:49.724
Rules is rules.
Let's see what I'm gonna put back.

16:49.849 --> 16:53.145
Okay, I need the Reynolds Wrap
and the bathroom tissue.

16:53.436 --> 16:56.983
I could do without the Triscuits,
but they sure are good.

16:57.900 --> 17:02.027
7- Up's the whole reason I came down here
in the first place. You know what?

17:02.320 --> 17:03.822
I'm not gonna need the V8,

17:03.947 --> 17:07.658
because I can just get some tomato juice
at the mini-mart down the street.

17:07.742 --> 17:09.703
It's a little more expensive,
but that's okay.

17:09.827 --> 17:11.871
I like to help out a small business.

17:11.997 --> 17:14.707
I hope it's okay if I pay you in pennies.

17:18.753 --> 17:20.838
Oh, God, a gutter? How clichй.

17:20.964 --> 17:22.672
I don't know what went wrong.

17:22.756 --> 17:25.382
I was just trying to live for the moment,
you know?

17:25.508 --> 17:29.723
Because life can end so abruptly
and there's nothing you can do to stop it.

17:29.847 --> 17:33.100
Is that why you've been on this path
to self-destruction?

17:33.224 --> 17:36.478
You know, Brian, as smart as you are,
you've got to accept the fact that

17:36.561 --> 17:39.398
there are some things in life
that you just can't control.

17:39.522 --> 17:42.900
You mean the way, the way
you can't control that messed up way

17:43.026 --> 17:46.111
that you laugh when you think
something's really, really funny?

17:46.237 --> 17:49.991
<i>Well, Hope, I don't understand why
these cookies are giving us all the fits.</i>

17:50.074 --> 17:53.828
<i>Well, no wonder, Faith.
That's not baking powder.</i>

17:54.079 --> 17:55.746
<i>It's sneezing powder.</i>

18:00.417 --> 18:04.295
<i>But, I already brought a whole batch
to the church bake sale.</i>

18:07.756 --> 18:10.928
<i>No wonder that priest kept saying,
'"Bless you. '"</i>

18:16.724 --> 18:17.934
Yes, and I accept that.

18:18.059 --> 18:21.394
Your problem is, you think that
just because you're not in control,

18:21.478 --> 18:25.234
nothing matters. That you don't matter.
But you know what?

18:25.358 --> 18:28.277
You matter to someone.
You matter big time.

18:31.197 --> 18:33.032
Hey, Meg. What are you doing here?

18:33.114 --> 18:35.951
Listen, Sarah,
I got to get something off my chest.

18:36.117 --> 18:38.787
- Yes!
- I need to open up.

18:38.911 --> 18:41.914
- Sweet.
- So get ready 'cause here it is.

18:42.039 --> 18:45.417
- My mom was right.
- What do you mean?

18:45.500 --> 18:47.587
- I'm not gay.
- What?

18:47.670 --> 18:51.007
So, all those rounds of golf we played,
those were all lies?

18:51.131 --> 18:52.425
I'm so sorry.

18:52.509 --> 18:55.303
For the first time in my life,
I felt like I belonged,

18:55.428 --> 18:59.473
and I wanted it to be true.
So I pretended to be something I'm not.

18:59.598 --> 19:01.768
You're going to choose
to be heterosexual?

19:01.892 --> 19:04.353
- I thought being gay wasn't a choice.
- Well, not for guys.

19:04.478 --> 19:07.481
It was wrong of me to mislead you.
I should go.

19:07.606 --> 19:10.984
That was awful. That was just awful.
What do you think, Mark?

19:11.108 --> 19:13.653
I don't know, man.
We didn't get the shots we need.

19:13.779 --> 19:15.488
Man, what do you think, Mike?

19:15.614 --> 19:17.740
I mean, if you saw action going on
in front of you,

19:17.824 --> 19:20.118
would you know instinctively
to center it in front of you?

19:20.244 --> 19:23.120
I don't know. Could someone take
my soda out of the icebox please,

19:23.204 --> 19:24.330
so it doesn't freeze?

20:45.741 --> 20:48.368
- Frank, there you are.
- Mia Farrow?

20:48.492 --> 20:51.747
What's this I hear about you up all night
with a baby and a dog?

20:51.872 --> 20:53.372
Oh, leave me alone.

20:53.497 --> 20:54.915
Get over here, young man.

20:55.000 --> 20:56.460
Damn it all.

20:56.461 --> 21:57.461
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru